+## Failed session initialization
+
+- When `beforeSession` throws an `Error`, the orchestrator awaits `onError(session, error)` and then `afterSession(session)` before rejecting with that same error, provided these hooks complete normally; both receive the original session and `onError` receives the original error, while user-input and model processing never start; `afterSession` is cleanup for an attempted turn, not proof initialization succeeded, so deployers must track their own allocations and tolerate partial or absent initialization because no new started flag is supplied ([validated by: awaits onError and afterSession before rejecting a failed beforeSession](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L7)).
+
